question_text:
What is the output of the following code? (ES6+)
```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 10);
}
```

What happens when you call 'foo()' and 'bar()' before their definitions in the code below?
```javascript
foo();
bar();
function foo() {}
var bar = function() {};
```

What is the output of the following code? (ES6+)
```javascript
if (true) {
  var a = 5;
  let b = 10;
}
console.log(a);
console.log(b);
```

What is printed when 'obj.log()' is called in the code below? (ES6+)
```javascript
const obj = {
  val: 42,
  log: function() {
    setTimeout(() => console.log(this.val), 10);
  }
};
```

What is the correct output sequence of the following code? (ES6+)
```javascript
console.log('1');
setTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('3'));
console.log('4');
```
